    "text": "PROVINCE OF BRMSki COLUMBIA \nORDER OF THE LIEUTENANT GOVERNOR IN COUNCIL \nOrder in Council No. \t1292 \t\n, Approved end Ordered OCT. 19.1995 \nExecutive Council Chambers, Victoria \nOn the recommendation of the undersigned, the Lieutenant Governor, by and with the advice and consent of the \nExecutive Council, orders that section 7 (2) of B.C. Reg. 479/76, the Guaranteed Available Income for Need Regu-\nlations, is amended by striking out \"or\" at the end of paragraph (d), by adding \"or\" at the end of paragraph (e) and \nby adding the following paragraphs: \n(f) is to a person \n(i) designated as Crown counsel under section 4 (1) of the Crown Counsel Act, or \n(ii) appointed as special prosecutor under section 7 (I) of that Act, \nbut only if the disclosure is for the purposes of a prosecution of an offence within the meaning of that \nAct, \n(g) is for the purpose of recovering a debt referred to in section 21 of the Act, or \n(h) is to the government of Canada, its departments, agencies or ministers or to the government of another \nprovince for the purpose of \n(i) complying with an agreement entered into under section 4 (1) of the Act, or \n(ii) research in support of policy development but only if the disclosure meets the conditions of \nsection 35 of the Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act. \nMinisterpyrSocialvices \t\nPres log Member of the Executive Council \n(This pars is for administrati If purposes only and is not port of the Order \nAuthority under which Order is made: \nAct and section:- \t Guaranteed Available Income for Need Act, s. 26 \nOther (specify):- \t o.c. 2531/76 \nOctober 5, 1995 \t\n/55/4 /95/99/aaa \n"
